cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "skgrad"
message: "If you use skgrad in academic work, please cite this software."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Hentschel"
    given-names: "Ludger"

repository-code: "https://github.com/LudgerHentschel/skgrad"
url: "https://ludgerhentschel.github.io/skgrad/"

license: "BSD-3-Clause"

keywords:
  - machine learning
  - scikit-learn
  - gradients
  - jacobian
  - sensitivity analysis
  - interpretability
  - integrated gradients
  - feature attribution

abstract: >
  skgrad computes analytic input derivatives of fitted scikit-learn
  estimators in closed form, without finite differences, automatic
  differentiation, or model conversion. Coverage includes linear
  models, kernel SVMs, multilayer perceptrons, and supported
  preprocessing pipelines.
